# Cloudflare Pages cache rules — prevent stale app shells after deploys.
# Every navigation route serves index.html via the SPA fallback (/, /lab, /feed,
# /perp/*, /portfolio, …), so ALL of them — not just the literal /index.html — must
# revalidate to pick up the CURRENT chunk hashes. Wallet in-app browsers (Zerion
# etc.) cache aggressively, and a rule scoped to /index.html alone never matched
# /lab, so the HTML went stale there. /* covers every route (incl. config.js, sw.js).
#
# ⚠️ A more specific rule does NOT win on Cloudflare: every matching rule applies, in
# file order, and a header set twice is JOINED with a comma (Pages docs; asset-server
# handler.ts appends when a key was already set). Without the "! Cache-Control" line,
# /assets/* shipped "no-cache, public, max-age=31536000, immutable" — and no-cache wins,
# so every visit re-checked every hashed file. The "!" line deletes the /* value first.
# Hashed files never change content, so they are safe to keep forever.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Search (Search Console Soft 404, 2026-10-19): these routes are the trading app itself (the
# Orderly SDK pages, account pages, DMs, ops). Their HTML is the empty app shell until JS and a
# wallet fill it, so they stay out of the index. Crawlable on purpose (no robots.txt Disallow),
# so Google can read this header. Indexed: /, /lab, /feed (+ calls and traders), /proof,
# /analyze, /token, /intel, /arena. Call permalinks that don't exist answer a real 404 from
# functions/feed/thesis/[wallet]/[id].js (headers here don't apply to Function responses).
/perp
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/perp/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/portfolio
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/portfolio/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
